FFmpeg reads every chapter edition of a Matroska file as one list and keeps each chapter that starts after
the last one kept, so a later edition's closing chapters were handed over after the first edition's. Each
edition is a whole alternative list, so only the default edition is read, as RFC 9559 20.1.2 defines it
and mpv picks it: the first flagged default, else the first. Still the case in FFmpeg 9.0.2.

